1 1 499.12403 391.98503 re
W
n
BT
0 0 0 rg
2 391.98503 Td
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(The analyst involved in the Active air Sampling plate setup, Simin Mohammad, and the analysts involved in reading the plate Sophia ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(Santamaria, were interviewed comprehensively. Their answers are recorded throughout this document.) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(The EM plates were stored in compliance with the supplier's recommendations, and their integrity was visually inspected prior to use. ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(Furthermore, the plates were confirmed to be within their valid expiration dates. All the supplies were thoroughly disinfected according to ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(MICRO-SOP-9 Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology. The functionality of both incubators were verified through a review of ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(data obtained from our comprehensive in-house continuous monitoring system.) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(Active air Sampling was performed by analyst Simin Mohammad during weekly environmental monitoring processing, in ISO 8 116, and ISO ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(7 116A, and ISO 7 116B on 07 May 2026 as per MICRO-SOP-2 - Environmental Monitoring of the Cleanroom Facility.) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(The plates were initially incubated at a temperature of 30–35°C in incubator E001031 for a minimum duration of 48 hours, commencing on ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(07 May 2026. Following completion of minimum of 48 hours of incubation on 11 May 2026, the plates were further incubated for minimum of ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(5 days, with the incubation concluding on 18 May 2026. Please see Table 1 for detailed information on the observations during respective ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(incubations. ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(Based on the observations in Table 1, since the CFU count exceeded the action level for the one of the Active air Sampling plates \(116A\), ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(the plate was submitted for Microbial Identification under ETX-260518-0254. The colonies were identified as Kocuria palustris \(Gram \(+\) ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(cocci\)) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(To observe if the organisms identified, were transient in nature or recurring, weekly environmental monitoring plates for the clean room were ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(bracketed to include the week before testing, the week of testing and week after testing as detailed in Table 2 \(please see attached\).) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(Environmental Monitoring Summary: Weekly environmental sampling for the previous week showed no growth for the active air and weekly ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(surface sample. Week of testing showed 748 CFUs in 116A ISO 7 and 1 CFU in 116B ISO 7 for active air identified as Kocuria palustris ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(\(Gram \(+\) cocci\). Lastly, the following week of testing showed 6 CFUs in ISO 8 116 for active air, 1 CFU on cart in ISO 8 116, and 2 CFUs ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(on floor in 116A ISO 7 identified as Gram \(+\) cocci, Gram-variable coccobacilli, Gram \(+\) cocci, Sporosarcina psychrophila, and Bacillus ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(pumilus. ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(During the interview with the analyst, they indicated that no obvious abnormalities or deviations in the testing procedure were observed. All ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(the samples were thoroughly disinfected prior to testing. Moreover, The CR116 was thoroughly cleaned and prepared before initiating the ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(testing as per MICRO-SOP-2 \(Environmental Monitoring of the Clean Room Facility\), and MICRO-SOP-9 \(Cleaning and Disinfecting ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(Procedure for Microbiology\).) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(Prior to the event, monthly cleaning and disinfection of the outermost ISO 8 Anteroom \(Suite 116\), the middle ISO 7 Buffer room \(Suite ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(116A\), the innermost ISO 7 clean room \(Suite 116B\), and its containing ISO 5 Biosafety Cabinets were performed on 26-Apr-2026 by ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(analysts Rey Estrada and Tamiru Kotisso as per MICRO-SOP-9 \(Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology\). It was documented ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(that all H2O2 indicators passed, confirming the efficient pre-event cleaning and established state of control of Suite 116. Furthermore, ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(subsequent monthly cleaning was performed on 31-May-2026 by analysts Tamiru Kotisso and Cuong Du with all H2O2 indicators passing, ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(confirming ongoing facility control. Additionally, cleaning and disinfecting was performed both prior to and after the testing process as per ) Tj
0 -8.928 Td
/Helv 8 Tf
(MICRO-SOP-9. ) Tj
ET
Q
EMC

endstream
